{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790098413,"nonce":"meVBxuFrYPvIIfKZySkZNkVH2Qs=","message":"Revised 2026-09-22 (f4bac00): (1) built-ins are code — schema.Builtins defines title (text), type, status (enum-with-category, defaults open/closed) and archived (bool); a field entity with a built-in key overrides values/name/on_open/on_close only (config-entity.md E4). (2) Fields carry two closed-set attributes this engine owns: on (issue|iteration) and role (assignee, estimate, start, target, due), so tooling finds assignee/dates/estimate by kind and role, never by key (E3). (3) multi-enum gets freeform; labels are a preset freeform multi-enum, not special. (4) kind list is now: text, enum-with-category, ordinal-enum, bool, number, date, identity, multi-enum, multi-identity, rank, iteration (configurable-schema.md D2). type validates against type entities — the one special case. (5) Types/relations are config entities, projected by this package from snapshots of those kinds; validation of issue writes goes in schema/ too and is called from cache/.","files":null}]}